# regression pin for #2163: the constant-time re-validation drain diverges too
#
# The monomorphizer is not the only engine that expands a generic family. Sema's
# per-instance re-validation (#2157) re-types each instance body under its
# concrete arguments, and a body that instantiates itself at a growing argument
# makes that drain grow without end as well - reached first, before lowering, and
# with a SEGFAULT rather than a hang, since re-validation substitutes structurally
# over an ever-deeper type.
#
# The `^` is what routes this case to that engine: an instantiation whose every
# argument is a public scalar is pruned from the re-validation worklist, so a
# secret in the program is what makes the drain record - and then chase - this
# family. Which engine refuses the family is what this case pins, not the chain's
# spelling: both engines name concrete arguments (`deepen[**u32]`) since #2302
# stopped lowering the template body, which was the only thing that could diverge
# through the template's own parameter.

fun deepen[T](x: ^u32) {
    deepen[*T](x);
}

fun main() i64 {
    var s: ^u32 = 1;
    deepen[u32](s);
    ret 0;
}
